******************************************************************
ABOUT MPP DEMO
******************************************************************

The MPP demo program will setup a virtual Greenplum database system on a 
single host. It creates and starts a MPP master instance and three 
segment instances within the same directory. Running MPP demo is a good 
way to test your initial installation before deploying the Greenplum database 
software on a multi-host array. It is also a good way to become familiar 
with the system without investing the time involved in a multi-host setup.

******************************************************************
BEFORE YOU BEGIN
******************************************************************

Before running MPP demo, you must at least 110 MB of free disk space, 
and have ports 5432, 10000, 10001, and 10002 free.

PREREQUISITES FOR SOLARIS USERS

* Make sure that make, tar, and a C compiler (gcc recommended) 
  is in your $PATH. 

* Verify that your $USER environment variable is set. 

* Greenplum recommends using the bash shell to run the MPP demo programs.

******************************************************************
RUNNING MPP DEMO
******************************************************************

1. Login as the MPP designated user (i.e. 'bgadmin').

	su - bgadmin

2. Go to the directory where you wish to unpack and run the MPP demo 
   program. This directory should have at least 110 MB of free space.

3. Unzip and untar mppdemo:

	tar -xvzf $MPPHOME/mppMgmt/demo/mppdemo.tar.gz

4. Go into the mppdemo directory you just untarred:

	cd mppdemo

5. Run make:

	make

6. If setup completes correctly, you will have a virtual Greenplum database 
   system running on the local host. You can connect to it using the 
   psql client program as follows:

	psql template1 -p 5432

7. To exit the psql client program:

	\q

8. See the Greenplum database User Guide for more information on using 
   your Greenplum database system.


******************************************************************
REMOVING MPP DEMO
******************************************************************

1. From the mppdemo directory run make clean:

	make clean

2. This will stop all Greenplum database demo server processes and remove all 
   files and directories created by the MPP demo program.

